This step generates the files needed to run the 13,312 scenario ensemble of drought scenarios. 

To run the large scenario ensemble we distributed the ensemble accross 60 cores on a high performance computing node. 
The "batch_job_script.py" script will generate multiple driver and q scripts to deploy multiple separate
jobs (1 on each core), each assigned a subset of the ensemble. The batch_job_script will also create a 
q_batch.sl file that will submit all of the jobs (driver_batch.sh and q.sl file pairs) with one command line call. 

The Inputs folder contains the required inputs for the pyartes model. 
The user needs to create an Output folder to save the model outputs. 

Workflow:
-Download Inputs folder and place in model directory
-Create Outputs folder and place in model directory
-If running scenarios in parallel. First generate batch and q scripts using "batch_job_script.py."
-If running locally Call pyaretes_pyomo_hpc_SR.py using:
    "python pyartes_pyomo_hpc_SR.py -i <path to input files> -o <path to output folder> -l <path to drought scenario file> -s"
    
    '-i', '--input', 'path to input directory'
    '-o', '--output','path to output directory'
    '-l', '--list', 'path to a csv file containing the scenarios'
    '-s', '--scenario','scenario row index to run'
